  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Upate carbon inequality</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This research will provide updated analysis of carbon inequality for Oxfam&#x2019;s work on climate and inequality. It will support Oxfam&#x2019;s Climate and Inequality Group&#x2019;s work of creating policy, research, advocacy, communication and/or public campaign tools for 2023. The aim of Oxfam&#x2019;s communication about this research will be to increase awareness of carbon inequality, highlighting an additional layer of climate justice and equality which is needed in global climate discussions.
The research will build on the previous carbon inequality work from 2020 and 2021. In the 2020  study, Stockholm Environment Institute (SEI) and Oxfam assessed global inequality between 1990 and 2015 as well as future global carbon inequality until 2100 under various scenarios.</narrative>
  </description>
